1
00:00:09,769 --> 00:00:14,181
Not everybody who needs to see
the work is somebody you employ.

2
00:00:14,638 --> 00:00:19,340
So you say so when they are invited, and
the product takes it seriously from then

3
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:19,514
on.

4
00:00:19,967 --> 00:00:26,009
Their whole authority is one role, in
the workspaces you shared with them. Never

5
00:00:26,009 --> 00:00:27,444
across the company.

6
00:00:27,897 --> 00:00:32,853
One of them watches. The other can also
raise a job, which is usually what a client

7
00:00:32,853 --> 00:00:33,748
actually wants.

8
00:00:34,201 --> 00:00:39,437
They hold no clock and no personnel
file. There is nothing there for them to be

9
00:00:39,437 --> 00:00:40,563
given by mistake.

10
00:00:41,029 --> 00:00:46,834
And the equipment the company owns is
closed to them, whatever else their role says.

11
00:00:47,286 --> 00:00:52,487
Next: the clients themselves —
the book of who you work for.

